an’s two-hour 20-minute running time could have been shaved by around a fifth, without losing a great deal.", "reference": "2017 September 19, Gwilym Mumford, “Kingsman: The Golden Circle review – spy sequel reaches new heights of skyscraping silliness”, in the Guardian:"}, {"text": "The acceleration was impressive, and these trains should allow TfW to look at shaving a few minutes off schedules here and there in the fullness of time, […].", "reference": "2023 April 19, Pip Dunn, “Jack of all trades... and master of most”, in RAIL, number 981, page 57:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(archaic, transitive) To be hard and severe in a bargain with; to practice extortion on; to cheat.", "tags": ["archaic", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(US, slang, dated, transitive) To buy (a note) at a discount greater than the legal rate of interest, or to deduct in discounting it more than the legal rate allows.", "tags": ["US", "dated", "slang", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(MLE, slang, transitive) To injure by employing a knife.", "tags": ["Multicultural London English", "slang", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Took one of the goons, the fuck they gonna do?\nShave him in the heart then the mandem smoke a zoot", "reference": "2021 June 26, Rackz LC, “War” (1:45 from the start):"}], "synonyms": ["stab", "chef", "ching", "juice", "shiv", "jook", "shank"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ʃeɪv/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "shaves", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "An instance of shaving.", "tags": [], "examples": ["I i